## `sidecar/bridge.py`

The line-delimited JSON sidecar that owns one browser session, reads a page as an indexed
action space, and executes one guarded operation at a time.

- Upstream: [`dsh-browser-use`](https://github.com/ricardochen1996/dsh-browser-use) v0.8.2,
  `sidecar/bridge.py`
- Upstream revision: `dfe8bfc5221cb6573c1a29bb258059f9a430cd0d`
- SHA-256 of the vendored file: `7a405211b17c774f939823e6f02fcb8cb5d3847b09f9ea3634928731cad3272f`
- Changes: the module docstring names this project as its host; plus the local patch in
  `patches/dsh-browser-use-diagnostics-and-daemon-loss.patch` — the browser enables `Runtime.enable`
  and `Network.enable` when a tab is attached, before a page loads, so `browser_console` reports the
  page's console output, exceptions and failed/4xx requests including those of its own load; a
  vanished Browser Harness daemon is answered with `lost_session` instead of a raw `OSError`; and
  end-of-input (a host that died without sending shutdown) stops the sidecar's own browser and daemon,
  so a SIGKILLed server cannot leak the Chrome it launched. Behaviour is otherwise unchanged.

## `vendor/jev_ultrafast-0.1.2-py3-none-any.whl`

The browser engine: a dynamic, indexed action space, a guarded executor, and the Jev/TypeSafe
policy loop. Imported as a library by `sidecar/bridge.py`; no engine source ships in this
package.

- Upstream: [`jev-ultrafast`](https://github.com/ricardochen1996/jev-ultrafast) v0.1.1,
